\title{Reviews out for Cloudburst}
\author{liamoc}
\import{table-macros}
\date{2026-09-28}
\p{We (being [Coro](https://corocanberra.com)) performed to a sizeable but not sold-out crowd for our second concert of the year, [Cloudburst](loc-005D). }
\figure{
  \<html:img>[loading]{lazy}[width]{480px}[src]{\route-asset{assets/cloudburst-photo.jpg}}%{}
 \figcaption{It was a delight to sing with Coro again.}
}
\p{I really enjoyed working with our guest director, [Roland Peelman](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roland_Peelman), and 
  it was great to have the opportunity to sing Tallis' \em{Lamentations of Jeremiah} ([Part 1](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ul8Hx1Fi-e8) and [Part 2](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fH_5SXZAtqY)). }
\figure{
    \<html:img>[loading]{lazy}[width]{300px}[src]{\route-asset{assets/coro-handbells.jpeg}}%{}
   \figcaption{The hand bells sounded great in Whitacre's [Cloudburst](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FS0MireFbi0).}
}
\p{The full programme is outlined in [this review](https://www.classikon.com/canberras-coro-performs-cloudburst-a-concert-of-dreams-visions-and-incantations/) from Jacqui Smith at classikON. }
\quote{
What a treat to hear a new choir (for me) performing such  a profound and deeply moving program, with excellent artistic programming, pace and delivery. I can’t wait to hear what they sing next.}
\p{There was also a more [nitpicky review](https://citynews.com.au/2026/coros-diverse-program-of-choral-works/) on CityNews.}
\p{I'll likely be singing again with a subset of Coro for a special Christmas concert. Stay tuned!}